.\" Man page for himalaya-mcp-setup
.\" Generated: July 2026
.TH HIMALAYA-MCP-SETUP 1 "July 2026" "himalaya-mcp 1.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
himalaya-mcp\-setup \- Manage the himalaya MCP server entry in Claude Desktop's config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B himalaya-mcp setup
[\fB--check\fR | \fB--remove\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds, verifies, or removes the
.B himalaya
MCP server entry in Claude Desktop's
.B claude_desktop_config.json
file.
.PP
When called with no flags, the command writes a new
.B mcpServers.himalaya
entry pointing at
.B dist/index.js
(alongside the CLI binary). The command preserves all
other
.B mcpServers
entries in the file.
.PP
This command is the legacy way to integrate himalaya-mcp with
Claude Desktop.
For new installs,
.BR himalaya-mcp-install-ext (the
.B .mcpb
Desktop Extension) is preferred.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Add the himalaya MCP server entry. Default when no flag is given.
.TP
.B --check\fR, \fBcheck
Verify Claude Desktop's config exists, contains the himalaya
entry, and that the entry's
.B dist/index.js
path exists on disk.
Exits 1 on any failure.
.TP
.B --remove\fR, \fBremove
Remove the himalaya MCP server entry. Idempotent: prints
"himalaya MCP server not in config. Nothing to remove." and exits 0
if the entry is already absent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
(macOS)
.br
.I ~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
(Linux)
.br
.I %APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json
(Windows)
.PP
The MCP server config file that
.B setup
modifies and
.BR --remove
cleans.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (entry added, removed, or already absent).
.TP
.B 1
.B --check
found a missing config, missing entry, or missing
.BR dist/index.js .
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time install:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp setup
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify the install:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp setup \-\-check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Uninstall:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp setup \-\-remove
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR himalaya-mcp (1),
.BR himalaya-mcp-install-ext (1)
